This study introduces a novel Hankel path integral representation for the Gamma function, which is valid across the entire complex plane. By employing this representation, we derive a new Hankel path integral formula for the Bessel function of the first kind, $J_{
u}(z)$, applicable for all complex values of $
u$ and $z$. Furthermore, we establish a connection between this newly derived formula and the classical Hankel path integral representation of $J_{
u}(z)$, which is traditionally defined for $	ext{Re}(
u) > -1/2$.
